;; Endeavor 152 rung 10 — ONE-SHOT MULTICAST, and the PTX that proves it fired.
;;
;; THIS RUNG IS THE DE-RISKING SPIKE FOR THE WHOLE ENDEAVOR.  A single multicast needs no ring,
;; no `empty` barrier, and no warp specialization: one workgroup in each cluster issues the
;; fetch, both workgroups await their OWN barrier, done.  That makes it the smallest kernel that
;; exercises the fact everything else is built on (Phase 0 / Q1) — that a multicast completes on
;; each destination workgroup's own mbarrier rather than only the issuer's.  If that assumption
;; is wrong, we want to know here and not after the ring and the handshake are built on it.
;;
;; WHY THE ASSERTION IS ON THE PTX AND NOT THE OUTPUT.  A `load-tile` that quietly declined to
;; multicast produces BYTE-IDENTICAL RESULTS — each workgroup simply does its own fetch of the
;; same tile.  No correctness test anywhere can distinguish the two.  The only evidence that the
;; mechanism engaged is in the emitted instruction, which is why CLAUDE.md says not to rely on
;; the validators to verify a new feature.
;;
;; WHAT THE VALIDATOR MUST LOOK FOR:
;;   - `cp.async.bulk.tensor` carrying `.multicast::cluster`
;;   - a ctaMask operand that is not zero and not all-ones for a 2-workgroup cluster
;;   - a leader guard around the issue (exactly one workgroup per group issues)
;;   - `mbarrier.arrive.expect_tx` still present in EVERY workgroup, not only the leader —
;;     each destination announces its own expected bytes even though it does not issue
;;
;; WHY THIS LOAD IS MULTICAST-ELIGIBLE.  The cluster is (2 1), so its axis is ROWS (grid-y).
;; The tile coordinates are `(0 grid-x)` — constant in the row axis — so both workgroups in a
;; cluster resolve to the SAME source tile and one fetch can serve both.  Change that first
;; coordinate to `grid-y` and the request must be refused; that is errors/11.
;;
;; NEW VALIDATOR REQUIRED: validate-ptx-multicast
;;
;; COMPILE-WITH[--ir-target=ptx --ir-target-arch=sm_90]: PASS
;; TEST-WITH[--ir-target=ptx --ir-target-arch=sm_90] : validate-ptx-multicast
;; SKIP-WITH[--differentiate]: "AD of :multicast is rung 9 of the plan — the adjoint of a multicast load is a cluster-wide reduction, and may ship as a refusal rather than a rule"

(def-type mat-t (matrix float :address-space :global :align :compact :contiguous-term :row-major))

(def-kernel mc_oneshot (A &out C)
  (declare #'(mat-t &out mat-t)
           (global-size :derive-from C :strategy :strided :tile-shape (8 8))
           (local-size  :set-to 32)
           (cluster-size :set-to (2 1)))
  (tile-stride C (8 8) (grid-y grid-x)
    (let ((tile (make-scratch-matrix float (8 8)))
          (bar  (make-async-barrier :mode :block)))
      ;; row coordinate is CONSTANT -> identical tile for both workgroups of the cluster
      (load-tile A tile (0 grid-x) :barrier bar :multicast true)
      (await bar)
      (store-tile tile C (grid-y grid-x)))))
